ition-by-daniel-mirchev\/","email":"contact@macadamgallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 489 11 96 21","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011001"},"en":{"name":"Something In The Air","shortdescr":"We are thrilled to announce that Bulgarian artist Daniel Mirchev will present next June 6 an inedited exhibition of eleven brand-new pieces at our new gallery space","longdescr":" \nDaniel Mirchev\u2019s sculptures play with both the figurative and the abstract and build his artistic world on the edge between them. Using plywood as his main material of choice, he contributes to the play between imaginary and real through woodcrafting. The material is interesting for the artist, because due to its layering, during its processing it creates new and independent lines and images that appear parallel to those created by him. This continuous play with forms leads to the perfect harmony between volume and lines.\n \nJoin us next Thursday, June 6, from 17h to 20h to discover Daniel Mirchev's universe in person.\n \nSomething in the Air by Daniel Mirchev\nOpening \/ Vernissage: Thursday, June 6, 17-20h\nVisit us from Thursday to Saturday, 10-18h\nMacadam Gallery, Rue du Charme 34, 1190 Forest\n \nContact us at contact@macadamgallery.com to sign up to receive the preview of the artist's catalogue before the opening.\n","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.macadamgallery.com\/exhibitions\/30-something-in-the-air-a-solo-exhibition-by-daniel-mirchev\/","email":"contact@macadamgallery.com","phone_contact":"+32 489 11 96 21","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011001"},"it":{"name":"Something In The Air","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.macadamgallery.com\/exhibitions\/30-something-in-the-air-a-solo-exhibition-by-daniel-mirchev\/","email":"contact@macadamgallery.com","phone_con